      - name: --ts-surface
        value: {r: 1, g: 1, b: 1, a: 1}
        note: 'A block: the opaque surface inside its rim (R12.5)'
      - name: --ts-surface-2
        value: {r: 0.95686275, g: 0.9411765, b: 0.9098039, a: 1}
        note: Buttons, chips and wells on a block
      - name: --ts-scrim
        value: {r: 0, g: 0, b: 0, a: 0.7}
        note: 'The scrim under a menu over the card (_3.2 step 8). The project renders
          in LINEAR colour, so an alpha blends in linear light: 0.5 left the card''s
          text behind at 181 of 247 (measured), still competing with the menu; 0.7
          recedes it to a frame (about 144)'
      - name: --ts-hero-fade
        value: {r: 0.95686275, g: 0.9411765, b: 0.9098039, a: 0.9}
        note: 
      - name: --ts-scrim-hero
        value: {r: 0.039215688, g: 0.031372547, b: 0.023529412, a: 0.94}
        note: 'The hero''s scrim behind its words (solid) and the tint of the ramp
          above them (hero_scrim.png holds the grade). The project blends in LINEAR
          light, so the alpha is chosen against the WORST pixel any picture can have,
          pure white: at 0.94 the ground stays at luminance 0.062 and the eyebrow
          (--ts-on-scrim-2) keeps 7.7:1, the title 9.3:1, over any picture (ThemeContrastTests;
          0.92 left the eyebrow 6.7:1 over The Lamp''s sky once its actions took
          one row, P4.4b part 2). The same in both modes: the hero is a picture'
